  "extraction_notes": [
    "Source PDF SHA-256 verified as 701ab4a06b0c85e1299e5f82bc5f29845e5a348fe368cc3b4f0574d6bba45bcb.",
    "BSS169 is an n-channel depletion-mode MOSFET; negative VGS(th) and negative VGS output-curve parameters are preserved as published.",
    "Transfer points were digitized from the single typical curve in Fig. 7. Output points were digitized from the flat, clearly separated typical curves in Fig. 5 at VDS = 4 V, 6 V, and 8 V.",
    "Capacitance points were digitized from the typical Ciss, Coss, and Crss traces in Fig. 12 with VGS = -10 V and f = 1 MHz. The tabulated typical values at VDS = 25 V are Ciss = 51 pF, Coss = 9 pF, and Crss = 4 pF; published MAX bounds are 68 pF, 13 pF, and 7 pF respectively.",
    "Published RDS(on) MAX bounds are preserved as separate maximum-source entries alongside the typical entries.",
    "Published IDSS is a minimum of 0.09 A at VGS = 0 V and VDS = 10 V; ID(off) maximums are 0.1 \u00b5A at 25 \u00b0C and 10 \u00b5A at 125 \u00b0C. These fields have no dedicated schema slots.",
    "Published body-diode VSD maximum is 1.2 V at VGS = -10 V and IF = 0.17 A; the schema slot contains the typical 0.79 V value. Published trr typical is 20.5 ns at VR = 50 V, IF = 0.12 A, and diF/dt = 100 A/\u00b5s.",
    "Thermal table publishes RthJA = 350 K/W for minimal footprint; no RthJC value is published."
  ],
